I agree - further dungeon branches are an excellent idea.  Perhaps
(potentially controversial idea alert) some of these branches could
join back up to the main dungeon as well?

Example: if you had an entrance to the Orcish Camp on level 8 of the
main dungeon and the Orcish Camp was 4 levels deep, there would be a
staircase at the bottom of the Orcish Camp which would take you back
to the main dungeon - say somewhere on level 11-13.

What I'm trying to do is evoke visions of a network of twisting,
turning passages with multiple routes to the bottom, rather that a
straight up and down dungeon with a couple of well-defined branches.

